      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DESPICABLE PEDRO (4) has been in the frame at his last two runs, most recently when third (22.77) in a Grade 5 over 400m at Maitland. Solid beginner and with a good start can find clear running from trap one. This looks easier and expected to bounce back. RUINATION (8) continued his winning form with another strong run after leading to make it two on the bounce, scoring by one length (17.80) at this track over 324m. Leading chance again. VILIAME (1) failed to come into contention last start at this track, but prior to that won by half a length at this track (17.95) beating Straight Out in a Mix 2/3 on August 13. Has good early burn and is suited drawn on the inside. Great chance to atone. MIRACULOUS TOMMY (3) was strongly fancied last time but finished third (17.76), beaten one length. Form from his last run is proving to be solid. Well placed and gets his chance.",
